    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The Widal Test is specifically used for the diagnostic confirmation of Typhoid fever caused by Salmonella typhi.",
        "BCG (Bacillus Calmette-Guérin) vaccine is administered at birth to confer immunity against Tuberculosis.",
        "Dengue fever causes severe thrombocytopenia, which presents as a sudden drop in blood platelet count.",
        "Vitamin D deficiency causes Rickets in children and Osteomalacia in adults, a frequent topic in competitive exam science sections."
      ],
      "id": "f27yzbv"
